%% System design written before implementation.
%% AnswerTable owns local sort/filter; parseAnswerBlocks owns bounded validation.
%% Empty state is derived from source and visible row counts, with no extra state.
%% Capacity: <=8 blocks, <=200 rows/table, <=20 columns. 10x is refused by parser;
%% first bottleneck is bounded DOM rendering. No distributed load or external calls.
%% Cache: existing mount fingerprint/WeakMap; replacement resets, disposal evicts.
%% Availability: invalid blocks show unavailable; text survives. No new dependency.
%% Postgres/N+1, queues, circuit breakers, rate caps, write idempotency: n/a,
%% UI uses already-loaded synchronous data, with zero network or writes.
%% Proof transport is sequential GET-only through app-release-reader: <=20 requests,
%% <=16 MiB, <=30s, no retries; first failure opens the circuit, exits 78 and emits
%% a receipt. Assets cache only for the run. Browser closes on every exit, including
%% late acquisition. No queue, persistence, or production write is introduced.
%% Consistency: source snapshot stays fixed during local filter/sort; changed answer
%% or identity retires local state. Each table owns independent controls.
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> RecordedEmpty: mount empty recorded table
  [*] --> Matching: mount recorded rows
  Matching --> NoMatches: absent local filter
  NoMatches --> Matching: clear filter preserves sort and sources
  Matching --> Matching: filter or sort
  NoMatches --> NoMatches: sort with no matches
  NoMatches --> Matching: reset clears sort and filter
  Matching --> Matching: reset clears sort and filter
  RecordedEmpty --> RecordedEmpty: filter or reset
  NoMatches --> NoMatches: identical mount preserves local state
  NoMatches --> Matching: replace answer identity or content
  Matching --> Invalid: invalid block replacement
  Invalid --> Matching: valid replacement
  Matching --> Disposed: dispose or retire session
  NoMatches --> Disposed: dispose
  RecordedEmpty --> Disposed: dispose
  Invalid --> Disposed: dispose
  Disposed --> Matching: remount
